---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "2026-05-23";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Privacy | Cocktails Guru"
    description="What data Cocktails Guru collects, and what it doesn't."
>
    <section class="mb-6 md:mb-8">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-4xl">
            Privacy notice
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Last updated {lastUpdated}.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground/90 md:text-base">
        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">Short version</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                No accounts, no login. No tracking pixels. The site does not
                sell or share any data, because there is no data to sell.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">What's stored on your device</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                Cocktail lists you create are saved in your browser's
                <code class="rounded bg-muted/40 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">localStorage</code>.
                Unit and serving preferences for the ingredients panel are
                stored the same way. None of it is ever sent to a server.
                Clear your browser data to delete it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">Service worker / offline cache</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                A service worker caches pages and assets so the site works
                offline. The cache lives in your browser. You can clear it
                from your browser's site-data settings.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">Analytics</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                When a Google Analytics property is configured (currently the
                presence of a measurement ID at build time), aggregated,
                non-personally-identifying traffic data is collected via
                Google Analytics. No analytics are loaded when the ID isn't
                configured.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">Hosting</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                The site is hosted as a static build. Standard server access
                logs (IP, user agent, referrer) may be kept by the host for
                operational purposes.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">External links</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                Recipe pages may link to product pages on third-party sites.
                Those sites have their own privacy policies.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-semibold">Contact</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">
                Questions, corrections, or removal requests:
                open an issue on
                <a
                    href="https://github.com/KiraLT/cocktails-guru/issues"
                    rel="nofollow noopener"
                    target="_blank"
                    class="text-primary hover:underline"
                >GitHub</a>.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
